  "question": {
    "text": "The reaction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Xe</mi><mrow/></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;gives a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Xe</mi></math> compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>. The number of moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HF</mi></math> produced by the complete hydrolysis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> is _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Xe</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><munder><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mrow><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>Xe</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>HF</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Number of moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HF</mi></math> formed by complete hydrolysis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
